INSERT INTO "blog_blocks" ("post_id", "position", "type", "data") VALUES
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 0, $s$itinerary_with_map$s$, $s${"itineraryId":"3a559e61-29f6-4102-99a9-41a7934cfd6f"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 1, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"We began our journey in 📌Chaguanas, exploring the vibrant heart of the town. The bustling Municipal Market, a kaleidoscope of colors and aromas, was a feast for the senses. We indulged in the local favorite – doubles – a savory treat that tantalized our taste buds."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 2, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1548","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1550","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1551","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1555","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1556","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1562","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1563","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1561"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 3, $s$two_column$s$, $s${"leftType":"image","rightType":"text","leftImage":"aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1565","leftImageAlt":"img1565","html":"We strolled through the town, admiring the architecture of buildings like the Lion House, a significant landmark with historical significance."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 4, $s$two_column$s$, $s${"leftType":"text","rightType":"image","rightImage":"aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1570","rightImageAlt":"img1570","html":"Next, we delved into the rich Indian heritage of Trinidad, visiting the 📌Serene Dattatreya Mandir Temple. Walking into the Dattatreya Mandir Temple, you really can't prepare for the feeling of standing there, face-to-face with that enormous statue of Lord Hanuman. It's truly massive, and it made me feel incredibly small in comparison. The whole atmosphere of the temple is just so peaceful and serene, despite the sheer scale of the statue. It's a powerful reminder that Indians are a significant part of Trinidad's population, and their culture deeply enriches the island. 💥 If you're hoping for a semi-private tour, I highly recommend arriving early, just like we did. That way, you'll find the entire place almost empty, which makes the experience even more impactful."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 5, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1569","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1572","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1575","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1576"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 6, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"And Then: The Magnificent Sea Temple 🌊🙏 After that incredibly moving visit to the Dattatreya Mandir Temple, we headed to our next stop 📌the Sewdass Sadhu Shiva Mandir Temple. This one is just unforgettable, dramatically situated right on the coast, seemingly rising out of the sea itself. It was a beautiful contrast to the inland temple, showing another facet of Trinidad's rich culture. While we were there, we even had a fascinating glimpse of a large Indian gathering for a private event, dressed beautifully in traditional Indian clothes."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 7, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1589","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1597","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1598","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1594","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1599","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1602","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1606","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1605"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 8, $s$two_column$s$, $s${"leftType":"text","rightType":"image","rightImage":"aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1608","rightImageAlt":"img1608","html":"After a delicious lunch at a local eatery, we ascended 📌San Fernando Hill, enjoying panoramic views of the surrounding landscape. The drive up was exhilarating, offering breathtaking vistas at every turn."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 9, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"The next stop was the legendary 📌La Brea Pitch Lake, a unique natural phenomenon. A local guide (check my tips section) expertly navigated us through the area, explaining this natural asphalt lake's fascinating history and geological wonders. He emphasized the importance of safety, highlighting the dangers of venturing into the pitch without proper guidance. Walking across the surface of the La Brea Pitch Lake was absolutely wild – it literally felt like I was treading on a bubbling black pudding! We had to be super careful with every step because our shoes could easily get stuck in the incredibly sticky pitch, especially since it was a hot day. Our guide was really serious about us sticking to the designated paths, and he even shared some fascinating (and a little bit chilling) stories about the locals. He told us how they've had to move their houses multiple times because of the bubbling, shifting earth underneath them! Can you imagine? Or about visitors who got stuck and lost inside these water bubbles... It was such a humbling experience, a powerful reminder of nature's incredible force and mystery, and how much we really need to respect it. Truly unforgettable."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 10, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1618","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1621","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1624","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1625","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1627","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1629","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1631","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1636"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 11, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"We made our way to the incredible 📌Caroni Bird Sanctuary. We timed it just right for the daily show – and trust me, you absolutely want to confirm your swamp tour departure time way in advance, because those limited spots vanish fast! Also, a quick tip 💥: bring cash, as many of the tour operators prefer it. This huge wetland is one of Trinidad's biggest, and it's just buzzing with all kinds of amazing birds. We even spotted some flamingos gracefully wading in the shallows, adding another splash of beautiful color to the landscape! But the real magic happened as the sun began to set. Suddenly, thousands upon thousands of Scarlet Ibises started flying in, coming back to their roosting spots. They literally painted the entire sky with the most vibrant, fiery red hues. It wasn't just a sight, it was a whole symphony of color and sound that's now absolutely etched into my memory. Truly breathtaking!"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3d38d7f7-9e99-4647-a3eb-28afd52c7fb1$s$, 12, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1653","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1654","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1672","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1670","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1693","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1688","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1699","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/4/IMG_1720"]}$s$::jsonb);
INSERT INTO "blog_posts" ("id", "country_slug", "post_index", "country", "country_code", "state", "title", "subtitle", "header", "description", "excerpt", "background_image", "tips_cta_copy", "tips_slug", "status", "published_at", "created_at") VALUES ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, $s$trinidad-and-tobago$s$, 5, $s$Trinidad and Tobago$s$, $s$TT$s$, NULL, $s$📍Tobago: Island Paradise Awaits$s$, $s$Tropical vibes, endless beaches, and pure relaxation. Tobago, you've captured my heart! 🌴🏖️$s$, $s$📍Beach & Rainforest: A Day of Contrasts🏖️🌲$s$, $s$Let's discover the unspoiled beauty of Tobago and experience paradise on this Caribbean gem. We'll dive into turquoise waters teeming with vibrant marine life, unwind on secluded, powdery white sand beaches, and explore lush rainforests.  Get ready to fall in love with Tobago's charm, tranquility, and endless natural wonders!$s$, $s$Tropical vibes, endless beaches, and pure relaxation. Tobago, you've captured my heart! 🌴🏖️🌲$s$, $s$aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1828$s$, $s$💥 Insider Tips: Your Key to an Unforgettable Trip (read more...)$s$, $s$trinidad-and-tobago$s$, $s$published$s$, '2025-08-02T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, '2025-08-02T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz);
INSERT INTO "blog_itineraries" ("id", "post_id", "position", "title", "map_embed_url") VALUES
  ($s$8f8d20ba-b0af-4963-810c-7396c4941773$s$, $s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 0, $s$Tobago_Beaches$s$, $s$https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m40!1m12!1m3!1d62602.293107024634!2d-60.69761350489427!3d11.287608406702049!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!4m25!3e0!4m5!1s0x8c4853e8fedee33d%3A0x1ef432cfd6352f48!2sCastara%20Bay%20Rd%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.279954!2d-60.6950764!4m5!1s0x8c4853e87af0512b%3A0x9bb0b51268c22197!2sCastara%20Beach!3m2!1d11.279833!2d-60.695929899999996!4m5!1s0x8c485154b47f626b%3A0x26ea8ba399baf10a!2sEnglishmans%20Bay%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.2918583!2d-60.6727874!4m5!1s0x8c4855caafa4f21b%3A0xf07a1bfe142e60ad!2sTobago%20Main%20Ridge%20Forest%20Reserve%2C%20Mason%20Hall%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.2737713!2d-60.6168974!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sus!4v1754186428058!5m2!1sen!2sus$s$);
INSERT INTO "blog_itinerary_items" ("itinerary_id", "position", "content") VALUES
  ($s$8f8d20ba-b0af-4963-810c-7396c4941773$s$, 0, $s$📌Castara Bay Rd$s$),
  ($s$8f8d20ba-b0af-4963-810c-7396c4941773$s$, 1, $s$📌Castara Beach$s$),
  ($s$8f8d20ba-b0af-4963-810c-7396c4941773$s$, 2, $s$📌Englishman's Bay$s$),
  ($s$8f8d20ba-b0af-4963-810c-7396c4941773$s$, 3, $s$📌Tobago Main Ridge Forest Reserve$s$);
INSERT INTO "blog_blocks" ("post_id", "position", "type", "data") VALUES
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 0, $s$itinerary_with_map$s$, $s${"itineraryId":"8f8d20ba-b0af-4963-810c-7396c4941773"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 1, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"As I mentioned in my insider tip, Tobago deserves more of your time if you're seeking a more laid-back pace focusing on beaches, rainforests, and relaxation. \nWe debated between the ⛴️ ferry and a 🛩️ flight but ultimately chose the ferry. We believed that savoring the journey, with its scenic views of the islands, was an integral part of the travel experience. Plus, the ferry ride wasn't significantly longer than a flight. We opted for the early morning ferry (6 AM) from Trinidad."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 2, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1949","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1945","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1946","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1771"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 3, $s$two_column$s$, $s${"leftType":"image","rightType":"text","leftImage":"aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1773","leftImageAlt":"img1773","html":"While sometimes prone to delays, the four-hour ferry ride offered a unique perspective, gliding past small, uninhabited islands as we sailed toward our destination. Upon arriving in Tobago, we collected our 🚙rental car and headed towards our hotel, but not before indulging in a delicious local lunch at a charming roadside eatery. This was the perfect start to our island adventure."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 4, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"The drive to 📌Castara Bay was an adventure in itself. The winding road demanded patience as we navigated past slow-moving buses and trucks."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 5, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1814","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1816","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1817","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1819"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 6, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"As we approached, the bay's beauty began to unfold, culminating in a breathtaking panorama. Castara Beach captivated us with its crescent shape and the unusual underwater shelf, creating a gradual and inviting entry into the turquoise waters. We couldn't wait to explore this idyllic corner of paradise.\nFrom there, we continued to explore another secluded beach, 📌Englishman's Bay, a hidden gem. This secluded paradise captivated us with its pristine white sand, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and a backdrop of lush green hills."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 7, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1830","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1831","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1832","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1837","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1839","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1841","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1845","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/5/IMG_1824"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 8, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"We reluctantly left the idyllic bay, eager to explore more before the fading light made driving on the winding roads too challenging. We headed to the 📌Main Ridge Forest Reserve🌲, the oldest protected rainforest in the Western Hemisphere. The drive through the lush green hills was a journey, offering glimpses of the island's diverse wildlife. We reached the reserve, and the air immediately felt cooler and fresher. The sounds of the rainforest created a sense of tranquility. We couldn’t spend more than an hour exploring the part of the trail (ℹ️ moderately difficult hike).\n As the light began to fade, we decided against continuing to 📌Argyle Falls. Driving on the winding roads with narrow shoulders in the dark presented a safety concern we weren't willing to risk.  💥 I recommend dedicating at least half a day to the forest."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$3893cddc-f455-4ac8-9e80-7cfe18b7037c$s$, 9, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"Tobago offers a diverse culinary scene, with many charming, smaller restaurants showcasing the island's unique flavors. To ensure a delightful dining experience, making reservations in advance is highly recommended, as these popular spots tend to fill up quickly."}$s$::jsonb);
INSERT INTO "blog_posts" ("id", "country_slug", "post_index", "country", "country_code", "state", "title", "subtitle", "header", "description", "excerpt", "background_image", "tips_cta_copy", "tips_slug", "status", "published_at", "created_at") VALUES ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, $s$trinidad-and-tobago$s$, 6, $s$Trinidad and Tobago$s$, $s$TT$s$, NULL, $s$📍Unveiling Tobago's Treasures$s$, $s$Tobago's Aquatic Gems: A Journey to the Fabled Nylon Pool & Lively Buccoo Reef 💙🐠✨$s$, $s$📌Unveiling Tobago's Treasures: Nylon Pool & Buccoo Reef🏝️🐠🪸$s$, $s$Dive into the crystal-clear magic of Tobago with us as we explore two of its most iconic underwater wonders: the enchanting Nylon Pool and the vibrant Buccoo Reef! This blog post takes you on a journey to discover the legendary "pool in the middle of the sea," where the water feels as soft as silk and promises rejuvenation. Then, plunge into the thriving ecosystem of Buccoo Reef, a protected marine park with colorful coral and an incredible array of tropical fish. Get ready to be mesmerized!$s$, $s$Beneath the Waves: Tobago's Iconic Water Adventures 💦🐠$s$, $s$aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1867$s$, $s$💥 Insider Tips: Your Key to an Unforgettable Trip (read more...)$s$, $s$trinidad-and-tobago$s$, $s$published$s$, '2025-08-03T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, '2025-08-03T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz);
INSERT INTO "blog_itineraries" ("id", "post_id", "position", "title", "map_embed_url") VALUES
  ($s$50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf$s$, $s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 0, $s$Nylon Pool & Buccoo Reef$s$, $s$https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m46!1m12!1m3!1d15657.059913678198!2d-60.84242305277283!3d11.168005974087151!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!4m31!3e0!4m5!1s0x8c49b3e87f71c9af%3A0x1632d2b72b7ec267!2sStore%20Bay%20Beach%2C%20Crown%20Point%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.1559032!2d-60.839817499999995!4m5!1s0x8c49b3962521cfbf%3A0x736df3b46cfd0921!2sPigeon%20Point%20Beach%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.1729402!2d-60.8382219!4m5!1s0x8c49b3005e884753%3A0x3237529e00e7259b!2sNylon%20Pool%2C%20Pigeon%20Point%20Road%2C%20Bon%20Accord%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.1647213!2d-60.840097799999995!4m5!1s0x8c49b3a169f6af53%3A0x16f361e956f4218b!2sBuccoo%20Reef%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.1822328!2d-60.8310901!4m5!1s0x8c49b3b761df1489%3A0x52f6ef57d1c9b49f!2sNo%20Man%E2%80%99s%20Land%2C%20Bon%20Accord%2C%20Trinidad%20and%20Tobago!3m2!1d11.168677299999999!2d-60.8250007!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sus!4v1754233605541!5m2!1sen!2sus$s$);
INSERT INTO "blog_itinerary_items" ("itinerary_id", "position", "content") VALUES
  ($s$50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf$s$, 0, $s$📌Store Bay Beach, Crown Point$s$),
  ($s$50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf$s$, 1, $s$📌Pigeon Point Beach$s$),
  ($s$50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf$s$, 2, $s$📌Nylon Pool$s$),
  ($s$50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf$s$, 3, $s$📌Buccoo Reef$s$),
  ($s$50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf$s$, 4, $s$📌No Man's land$s$);
INSERT INTO "blog_blocks" ("post_id", "position", "type", "data") VALUES
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 0, $s$itinerary_with_map$s$, $s${"itineraryId":"50283123-e810-46f1-b611-20c60920a3bf"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 1, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"We were excited to explore Tobago's underwater wonders today! We met our tour guide at 📌Pigeon Point Beach (ℹ️ entrance fee applies), passing by 📌Store Bay Beach, where locals enjoyed a leisurely swim. The vibrant stalls selling local art along the way added a touch of local color. The beach is simply idyllic, think soft white sand, swaying palm trees, and clear turquoise water. It's truly a picture-perfect Caribbean paradise! Note, on the way to Pigeon Point, you'll spot some charming local stalls selling all sorts of vibrant, local art. It's a great chance to grab a unique souvenir!"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 2, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1853","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1854","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1860","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1852","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1851","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1867 2","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1889","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1868"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 3, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"Our first stop, the 📌Nylon Pool, named after Princess Margaret, was a magical experience. She likened the pool's crystal-clear water to the transparency of nylon, a fitting description for its remarkable clarity. Locals believe that swimming in these turquoise waters possesses rejuvenating powers. The crystal-clear water was simply mesmerizing."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 4, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1861","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1911","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1908","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1916"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 5, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"We then explored the vibrant 📌Buccoo Reef, encountering a dazzling array of marine life. It was a living, breathing kaleidoscope down there – the corals were vibrant, and I just kept seeing schools of bright, colorful fish zipping past in every direction. It truly felt like an underwater wonderland!"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 6, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1893 2","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1894","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1900","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1898"]}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 7, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"Our boat trip had another fantastic surprise: a stop at No Man's Land, a secluded, pristine white-sand beach accessible only by boat! It wasn't on our original plan, but it turned out to be this incredible, tiny slice of paradise. The water was just ridiculously clear, and the best part? Locals were right there, selling the freshest seafood, which made for the perfect, spontaneous moment of pure relaxation and a delicious treat, before returning to Pigeon Point to relax and enjoy the afternoon."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$1d890bb4-3c0b-4c83-8e30-eb305bcd4748$s$, 8, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1923","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1922","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1939","aroundtheworld50s/blog/trinidad-and-tobago/6/IMG_1885"]}$s$::jsonb);
INSERT INTO "blog_posts" ("id", "country_slug", "post_index", "country", "country_code", "state", "title", "subtitle", "header", "description", "excerpt", "background_image", "tips_cta_copy", "tips_slug", "status", "published_at", "created_at") VALUES ($s$58add61d-ba33-438e-bef4-cbbe75717088$s$, $s$united-states-new-york$s$, 1, $s$United States$s$, $s$US$s$, $s$New York$s$, $s$📍Body Painting, Union Square, Manhattan$s$, $s$Final Canvas: Reliving the Body Painting Magic in Union Square! 🎨✨🗽$s$, $s$📍 Body Painting, Union Square$s$, $s$Remember that unforgettable experience of becoming a living work of art? This post takes you back to our last incredible body painting adventure right in the heart of NYC's Union Square! We're looking back at the vibrant colors, the incredible artists, and the amazing energy of turning public space into a canvas.  🖌️🌟$s$, $s$✨A Farewell to Fantastic: Witnessing the Last NYC Body Painting Day🎨$s$, $s$aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0731$s$, $s$💥 Insider Tips: Your Key to an Unforgettable Trip (read more...)$s$, $s$united-states-new-york$s$, $s$published$s$, '2025-08-10T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, '2025-08-10T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz);
INSERT INTO "blog_blocks" ("post_id", "position", "type", "data") VALUES
  ($s$58add61d-ba33-438e-bef4-cbbe75717088$s$, 0, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"After over a decade of transforming Union Square into a vibrant canvas of human artistry, New York City's annual Body Painting Day ended on July 23, 2023. This final edition was a dazzling spectacle, a vibrant tapestry of colors and creativity as artists meticulously transformed nude models into living masterpieces."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$58add61d-ba33-438e-bef4-cbbe75717088$s$, 1, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"Everywhere we looked, we saw bodies transforming – it was truly mind-blowing to see intricate patterns, wild and fantastical creatures, and vibrant abstract designs come to life right before our eyes. It was a powerful celebration of the human form, showcasing the incredible talent and dedication of every single artist involved.\n\nEach person became their unique masterpiece, a fleeting piece of art that everyone could witness. As the day progressed, the energy in Union Square continued to build, a truly vibrant testament to the power of art and the resilience of the human spirit."}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$58add61d-ba33-438e-bef4-cbbe75717088$s$, 2, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0482","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0485","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0487","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0492","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0494","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0542","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0518","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0521","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0487","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0544","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0554","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/1/IMG_0527"]}$s$::jsonb);
INSERT INTO "blog_posts" ("id", "country_slug", "post_index", "country", "country_code", "state", "title", "subtitle", "header", "description", "excerpt", "background_image", "tips_cta_copy", "tips_slug", "status", "published_at", "created_at") VALUES ($s$88d35806-7dd9-43df-8d28-2b17ca69980d$s$, $s$united-states-new-york$s$, 2, $s$United States$s$, $s$US$s$, $s$New York$s$, $s$📍4th of July fireworks Over the Hudson$s$, $s$✨A Night of Stars & Stripes: Catching the 4th of July Fireworks on the Hudson River🎇$s$, $s$📍A 4th of July NYC Spectacle$s$, $s$Oh, that 4th of July night on the Hudson River! It's one of those experiences you don't forget.  I'm taking you back to the sheer magic of watching those spectacular fireworks light up the New York City skyline. From the buzzing energy of the crowds to finding that perfect spot to witness the display, I'll share all the highlights of what truly felt like a quintessential NYC summer moment. I love fireworks so much, and this display was everything!$s$, $s$4th of July Spectacle: Fireworks on the Hudson! 🎆🗽🇺🇸$s$, $s$aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_1138$s$, NULL, NULL, $s$published$s$, '2025-08-16T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, '2025-08-16T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz);
INSERT INTO "blog_blocks" ("post_id", "position", "type", "data") VALUES
  ($s$88d35806-7dd9-43df-8d28-2b17ca69980d$s$, 0, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"The anticipation was absolutely palpable. We arrived in the area around 5 PM, determined to snag a great spot along the Lower East Side. It took us more than 30 minutes just to walk from the station because so many streets were closed! We had to follow the police directions to figure out where we were even allowed to enter the viewing area. Even by 5 PM, people were already stretched out along the river, totally committed to getting the best view. Despite the crowds, we managed to find a good spot, even able to lean right on the railing! The riverfront slowly filled up, everyone eager to witness the legendary Macy's fireworks display.\n\nAnd then, just like that, it began. A full-on symphony of color just erupted over the river, painting the entire night sky. The fireworks display was breathtaking, dazzling against the iconic city skyline. I remember just being completely in awe as each explosion arced across the sky, reflecting perfectly in the waters of the Hudson below. It truly felt like the city itself was part of the show, not just a backdrop.\n\nFor me, that display was more than just pretty lights; it was a powerful reminder of why I love New York City so much – that incredible sense of power and celebration. It captures the spirit of Independence Day in such a unique way.\n\n💥Pro Tip: If you ever go, arrive early! Seriously, securing a good spot along the riverfront is key to truly soaking in the show without any obstructions.\n\nHave you ever witnessed the Macy's 4th of July Fireworks display? What was your favorite part? Share your experience in the comments below!"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$88d35806-7dd9-43df-8d28-2b17ca69980d$s$, 1, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_2288","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_2287","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_2286","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_2285","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_2284","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_0786","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_1136","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_1137","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_1138","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_1132","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/2/IMG_1135"]}$s$::jsonb);
INSERT INTO "blog_posts" ("id", "country_slug", "post_index", "country", "country_code", "state", "title", "subtitle", "header", "description", "excerpt", "background_image", "tips_cta_copy", "tips_slug", "status", "published_at", "created_at") VALUES ($s$a5186724-1ce2-4a97-ac06-3591d9ebac1e$s$, $s$united-states-new-york$s$, 3, $s$United States$s$, $s$US$s$, $s$New York$s$, $s$📍Fireworks Over the Hudson$s$, $s$✨A Night of Stars & Stripes: Catching the 4th of July Fireworks on the Hudson River🎇$s$, $s$📍Fireworks Over the Hudson: A 4th of July NYC Spectacle$s$, $s$Oh, that 4th of July night on the Hudson River! It's one of those experiences you don't forget. I'm taking you back to the sheer magic of watching those spectacular fireworks light up the New York City skyline, from the buzzing energy of the crowds to finding that perfect spot to witness the display, an NYC summer moment. I love fireworks so much, and this display was everything!$s$, $s$A 4th of July NYC Spectacle over the Hudson River$s$, $s$aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_1137$s$, NULL, NULL, $s$published$s$, '2025-08-17T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz, '2025-08-17T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz);
INSERT INTO "blog_blocks" ("post_id", "position", "type", "data") VALUES
  ($s$a5186724-1ce2-4a97-ac06-3591d9ebac1e$s$, 0, $s$text$s$, $s${"html":"The anticipation was palpable. We arrived in the area around 5 PM, determined to snag a great spot along the Lower East Side. It took us more than 30 minutes to walk from the station because so many streets were closed! We had to follow the police's directions to figure out where we were allowed to enter the viewing area. Even by 5 PM, people were already stretched out along the river, totally committed to getting the best view. Despite the crowds, we managed to find a good spot, even able to lean right on the railing! The riverfront slowly filled up, everyone eager to witness the legendary Macy's fireworks display.\n\nAnd then, just like everyone was holding their breath, it began. A symphony of colors erupted over the river, painting the entire night sky. The fireworks display was breathtaking, dazzling against the iconic city skyline. I remember just being completely in awe as each explosion arced across the sky, reflecting perfectly in the waters of the Hudson below. It truly felt like the city itself was part of the show, not just a backdrop.\n\nFor me, that display was more than just pretty lights; it was a powerful reminder of why I love New York City so much – that incredible sense of collective wonder and celebration. It captures the spirit of Independence Day in such a unique way.\n\n💥Pro Tip: If you ever go, arrive early! Seriously, securing a good spot along the riverfront is key to truly soaking in the show without any obstructions.\n\nHave you ever witnessed the Macy's 4th of July Fireworks display? What was your favorite part? Share your experience in the comments below!"}$s$::jsonb),
  ($s$a5186724-1ce2-4a97-ac06-3591d9ebac1e$s$, 1, $s$image_grid$s$, $s${"images":["aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_2284","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_2285","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_2286","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_2287","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_2288","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_0786","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_1136","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_1137","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_1132","aroundtheworld50s/blog/united-states-new-york/3/IMG_1135"]}$s$::jsonb);
INSERT INTO "tips" ("id", "slug", "country", "country_code", "state", "title", "description", "status", "published_at") VALUES ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$trinidad-and-tobago$s$, $s$Trinidad and Tobago$s$, $s$TT$s$, NULL, $s$Trinidad and Tobago Travel Tips$s$, NULL, $s$published$s$, '2026-04-12T21:51:34.489Z'::timestamptz);
INSERT INTO "tip_sections" ("tip_id", "section_key", "content", "enabled", "position") VALUES
  ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$essential_tips$s$, $s$<p>🇹🇹  <strong>Trinidad - Insider Tips ⁉️</strong></p> <p>☀️ <strong>Time to Visit</strong> The best time to visit is from December to April for the dry season. While it's wise to avoid hurricane season (June-November), we took a chance in early October and were lucky enough to enjoy fantastic weather! 🤞</p> <p>✈️ <strong>Flights</strong> - Caribbean Airlines offers convenient morning flights from NYC, giving you an entire afternoon to explore this vibrant island nation.</p> <p>⏳ <strong>Focusing Your Time</strong> - We decided to spend 10 days exploring the twin 🏝️islands of Trinidad & Tobago, splitting our time evenly between them. Looking back, we wholeheartedly recommend focusing more on Tobago. This smaller island boasts breathtaking beaches, lush rainforests, and a more relaxed pace. While both islands offer unique experiences, Tobago truly captivated our hearts.</p> <p>🏌️ <strong>Guided tour</strong> - When visiting the La Brea Tar Pits, you'll encounter local guides offering their services. These knowledgeable guides provide fascinating insights into the history and paleontology of the site, enriching your experience. But be sure to agree on a fee beforehand for a smooth and enjoyable visit.</p> <p>ℹ️ <strong>Driving tips</strong> (in case you decide to rent a car) - Driving in the islands presents unique challenges. Firstly, remember to drive on the left-hand side of the road. Secondly, be prepared for sudden stops by locals. Be cautious, as most roads lack proper shoulders and usually have dips or trenches. For your safety, we recommend driving during daylight hours.</p> <p><strong>Tobago: Visiting Nylon pool, and Buccoo</strong> - We initially considered booking our Nylon Pool and Buccoo Reef tour through Viator, but we quickly discovered that many local operators offer similar experiences at significantly lower prices. We booked our tour through a hotel recommendation, but exploring the beach itself will likely reveal a variety of tour operators offering competitive rates.</p> <p>💲 <strong>Currency</strong>: Trinidad and Tobago Dollar (TTD) - US dollars widely accepted.</p> <p>🗣️ <strong>Language</strong>: English is the official language, but you'll hear lots of local slang and expressions.</p> <p>💁 <strong>Tipping</strong>: 10-15% at restaurants, round up for taxi drivers</p> <p>🛜 <strong>Internet</strong>: You'll find 🛜 at most hotels and cafes. For consistent connectivity, consider grabbing a local SIM card or purchasing an international package from your home provider</p>$s$, TRUE, 0),
  ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$budget_planning$s$, NULL, FALSE, 1),
  ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$food_dining$s$, $s$<p>🇹🇹🌶️ <strong>Food</strong>: Prepare your taste for a vibrant adventure in Trinidad and Tobago, where the food is as rich and diverse as its culture! This twin-island nation offers a tantalizing array of dishes and a delicious fusion of African, Indian, Creole, and even Chinese influences.  Prepare your taste buds for a vibrant adventure in Trinidad and Tobago, where the food is as rich and diverse as its culture! This twin-island nation offers a tantalizing array of dishes and a delicious fusion of African, Indian, Creole, and even Chinese influences. One absolute must-try you'll find at nearly every street corner is Doubles. These are deceptively simple yet incredibly flavorful street foods. We quickly became obsessed, grabbing them from street stands whenever we could.</p>$s$, TRUE, 2),
  ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$transportation$s$, $s$<p>🚌 <strong>Transportation</strong> - 🚕'Maxi Taxis' or 🛻'PHs': These are shared rides where locals stand by the roadside and flag down passing vehicles. While affordable, they may not be the safest option for tourists, especially outside city limits.  Formal 🚖Taxis are typically booked through your 🏨hotel. While more expensive, they offer a safer and more reliable option for getting around.</p> <p>🚗 <strong>Renting a car</strong> - Most sites and even locals advise against renting a car due to concerns about driving conditions and local culture. However, after experiencing the limitations of public transportation and the high cost of taxis, we decided to rent a car. This was the best decision, allowing us to explore the island at our own pace. ⚠️A crucial tip: Always take 📷photos of the rental car, including the wheels, to avoid any disputes upon return.</p>$s$, TRUE, 3),
  ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$accommodation$s$, $s$<p><strong>Trinidad</strong>:</p> <p>Convenience to attractions was our top priority. We found that staying near Queen's Park Savannah was a game-changer. This massive green space isn't just great for a leisurely walk; it's also centrally located, giving you easy access to so many parts of the city. Look for hotels surrounding the Savannah – you'll be right at the heart of the action, ready to explore! our hotel, [The BRIX, Autograph Collection](https://expedia.com/affiliate/Zm1VD21). We selected this 🏨for its upscale accommodations, great deal, and proximity to key attractions.</p> <p>If you're opting for private rentals  🏠 or guesthouses, make sure they have good security features like strong locks and grills, especially if they're in isolated locations.</p> <p><strong>Tobago</strong>:</p> <p>We booked [hotel](https://expedia.com/affiliate/ghdYxIR) at Crown Point, the most developed area on the island, close to the airport (ANR Robinson International Airport) and Pigeon Point Beach with easy access to restaurants, bars, and popular tourist activities.</p> <p>If renting a private villa, especially in more isolated areas, ensure it has robust security measures.</p>$s$, TRUE, 4),
  ($s$0e623603-f1fa-4e99-971a-dd8661ccae7f$s$, $s$safety_health$s$, $s$<p><strong>Trinidad</strong>:</p> <p>Walking around 🚶Many roads lack proper curbs and may have sudden dips or trenches. Avoid walking at night, especially in less populated areas, and always be aware of your surroundings, as vehicles drive on the left-hand side of the road.</p> <p>Avoid high-crime areas: Steer clear of neighborhoods like Laventille, Morvant, Sea Lots, Beetham, and parts of East Port of Spain (especially south Charlotte Street and Piccadilly Street), particularly after dark.</p> <p>Be cautious at night: Even in safer areas, avoid walking alone in poorly lit or isolated spots, including certain parts of downtown and Queen's Park Savannah after dark.</p> <p><strong>Tobago</strong>:</p> <p>While Tobago is generally safer than Trinidad, common sense precautions apply. Avoid walking alone on deserted beaches or isolated areas, especially after dark.</p> <p>Be very cautious about booking isolated private villas 🏠 without confirmed, adequate 24-hour security.</p>$s$, TRUE, 5);
